		{
			"id": "tJ889kLqTnaAEabQB",
			"name": "Augmetic Arm, Menial Pattern",
			"reference": "B40",
			"local_notes": "Arm ST +2 (Lifting ST +2 and Striking ST +2, applied by the sheet); DR 2 to the arm. GCS applies these to the whole character, so for a single prosthetic arm use them for that arm only (the second arm has no bonus, and DR covers only the augmetic arm's hit location).\n\nLore: The cheap, mass-produced limb replacement issued to menial serfs, manufactorum labourers and low-ranking Mechanicus staff who have lost an arm to an industrial accident: a servo-motor and a counterweight under a metal or plastek shell, strong enough for its job and no more.\n\nDesign: Arm ST +2 (B40, 5/level, 10 points) for the servo-assisted grip and lift, plus DR 2, Partial (single limb) -60% (2x5=10, x0.4=4). 14 points. This is a trait built from Basic Set abilities, not a renamed Ultra-Tech/Bio-Tech catalogue \"bionic arm.\"",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 14,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"arm"
					],
					"amount": 2
				},
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "lifting_st",
					"amount": 2
				},
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "striking_st",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tOH9ElLd49DM8z2M3",
			"name": "Augmetic Arm, Combat Pattern",
			"reference": "B40",
			"local_notes": "Arm ST +6 (Lifting ST +6 and Striking ST +6, applied by the sheet); DR 6 to the arm. GCS applies these to the whole character, so for a single prosthetic arm use them for that arm only.\n\nLore: The heavier pattern carried by Skitarii, veteran Enginseers, and any Tech-Priest expecting to use the limb itself as a weapon: cabled myomer bundles under an armoured casing, powerful enough to break a man's grip or punch through a hab door.\n\nDesign: Arm ST +6 (B40, 5/level, 30) + DR 6, Partial (single limb) -60% (6x5=30, x0.4=12) = 42 points.",
			"tags": [
