		},
		{
			"id": "tdg8nm8BHr94dsqNZ",
			"name": "Augmetic Leg, Menial Pattern",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR 2 to the leg (the sheet applies it to the leg location; use it for the augmetic leg only); the prosthetic joint doesn't fatigue or cramp.\n\nLore: A basic replacement leg for a menial or low-ranking adept: functional, unglamorous, and common wherever industrial accidents are common.\n\nDesign: DR 2, Partial (single limb) -60% (2x5=10, x0.4=4) + a 1-point Perk (B9) for a joint that never tires or cramps the way a natural knee does over a long shift. 5 points. (Basic Set has no dedicated \"Leg ST\" advantage the way it has Arm ST for arms; a single prosthetic leg does not meaningfully raise Move or damage on its own, so this entry is DR plus a flavor Perk rather than an invented attribute bonus.)",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 5,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"leg"
					],
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t-qAZDx0JazQGiqlJ",
			"name": "Augmetic Legs, Combat Pattern (Matched Pair)",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR 6 on both legs; Basic Move +1 from servo-assisted stride.\n\nLore: Skitarii Rangers and Vanguard are routinely fielded with both legs replaced outright rather than one at a time; the matched pair's synchronized actuators give a longer, steadier stride than a single prosthetic bolted onto an otherwise natural gait.\n\nDesign: DR 6, Partial (both legs, a larger fraction of the body than a single limb) -50% (6x5=30, x0.5=15) + Basic Move +1 (B17, 5 points/level) = 20 points. Buying only one leg from this pair does not grant the Move bonus; use Augmetic Leg, Menial Pattern for a single prosthetic instead.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"leg"
